If you're looking for intrinsics, how about ones that make you appear to be
one of the damned souls that should inhabit Hell? Possibly gives you a %
chance that , for instance, undead won't bother you, thinking you belong
here? The demons would still attack you, since that's their job (tormenting
the damned).

If you're going to add creatures, adding Cerberos to the entrance of Hell
might be an idea; You have to get past him, but once he drops to a certain
number of hit points, he runs away to give the alarm to .... someone. You
then have to chase him through Hell and kill him before he gives the alarm.
Failure to do so could wipe out your "look_like_a_damned_soul" intrinsic.
However, since Cerberos guards the entrance to Hell, he shouldn't know his
way through it, so that he has to search each level to find the way down -
makes it easier to catch up with him. This potentially also adds some
urgency to your trip through Hell.

I agree that Gehennom is a little boring with those endless mazes (though I
can only get there in explorer mode still :-) How about adding some
variety? So for example, have a couple of levels of mazes, then maybe a
couple of levels of mines, then a couple of bigrooms, etc? Actually, if
you're going to add Cerberos, above, possibly also add a "River Styx"
level? Possibly with an intrinsic you can get to swim across? (The Boat man
should be willing to ferry across mortals, should be a formidible opponent,
and should go after anyone who tries to swim/float across).

What do you think?

